"""The LINZ Data Service's catalogue as the lane holds it (Arthur, 4 November 2026, ruling 142: "Get LINZ and all
available information and put it all in the database"): every layer and table the service's WFS capabilities list
(1,856 on 4 November 2026) that bears on land, titles, ownership, parcels, addresses, property, valuation or survey,
222 of them, with what the inventory read of each (docs/research/linz-everything-2026-11-04.md): its typeName, the
lane's name for it, its title, its licence (`cc` CC BY 4.0, `personal` the LINZ Licence for Personal Data 2.3), its
rows (WFS `numberMatched`, 4 November 2026), its geometry column, the columns its pages are sorted on, and its tranche:

  1  the title spine and what the geometry join needs: parcels and the title-parcel association (weekly)
  2  titles, estates, memorials, properties and valuation, Crown land, places, roads, buildings (weekly)
  3  the Full Landonline Dataset and the titles' own shapes (monthly)
  4  the survey's measurements: observations, marks, vectors, nodes, coordinates, adjustments (quarterly)
  None  not taken, and `why`

A tranche-1 entry named as a legacy source (titles, owners, place_names, the property spine, addresses) is read by
the lane's typed reader (capture.SOURCES); every other taken entry is read whole, every attribute and the geometry,
into `linz_private` (capture.WHOLE). Generated from the inventory, then kept by hand: a new layer is a new line.
"""

